From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: switch immersive mode and return to macOS from the keyboard

Applies after all other Try Omarchy Cocoa patches.

Immersive full screen hides the Mac menu bar and Dock, and full grab gives
every focused key to the guest, so there was no keyboard way back to macOS
short of shutting Omarchy down, and immersive mode could only be chosen at
launch.

Add two host shortcuts to the existing Control-Option table (where
Control-Option-1..9 and Control-Option-G already belong to QEMU):

- Control-Option-Escape switches between immersive full screen and a
  resizable window, the two choices the launcher offers. Any full screen leaves for a
  window with immersive off; a window enters full screen with immersive on.
  The VM keeps running and the guest follows the window size. The launcher's
  saved setting is unchanged, and a switch requested mid-transition is
  ignored.
- Control-Option-Shift-Escape hides Try Omarchy, unless a full-screen
  transition is running. Its full-screen Space goes away, and app deactivation already
  releases the keyboard and every key held in the guest. Clicking it in the
  Dock or Command-Tab brings it back.

Full grab is unchanged, so Command stays with the guest in both presentations.

Both run from the main queue after the key event returns, outside the BQL,
because AppKit window transitions call back into code that takes it. Key
auto-repeat is consumed without acting again. If a switch's transition fails,
the immersive state goes back to what it was. A View menu item, labeled with
the shortcut, shows and changes the current state while the menu bar is
visible.

